#%RAML 1.0
title: Platform Lifecycle Orchestrator API
version: v1
mediaType: application/json
description: |
  The Platform Lifecycle Orchestrator API enables AI agents and automation tooling to manage the full lifecycle
  of MuleSoft application upgrades — from runtime and Java version assessments through automated code changes,
  pull request creation, and deployment tracking. Use this API to orchestrate zero-touch or low-touch
  platform migrations at scale.

types:

  ChangePlan:
    type: object
    properties:
      targetRuntime:
        type: string
      targetJavaVersion:
        type: string
      filesToChange:
        type: array
        items: string
      hasApiPolicies:
        type: boolean
      hasCustomJavaCode:
        type: boolean
      hasLookupFunction:
        type: boolean
      missingFromMatrix:
        type: array
        required: false
        description: |
          Connectors/modules the app declares in its pom that the compatibility matrix does
          NOT cover, so they could not be auto-pinned for Java 17. Each entry is a
          { groupId, artifactId } pair. Non-empty results also raise a Slack alert and a
          warning in the AssessmentResult; extend the matrix and reapply to pin them.
        items:
          type: object
          properties:
            groupId: string
            artifactId: string
      connectorGaps:
        type: array
        required: false
        description: |
          Matrix connectors inherited from a parent/BOM (or transitively version-locked, e.g.
          mule-sockets-connector pulled by HTTP) that are BELOW the Java 17 target and were NOT
          pinned in the app pom — only connectors already carrying a <version> in the app pom are
          pinned. Each entry is { groupId, artifactId, from, to }. These are also surfaced in
          `warnings`; resolve them by updating the parent/BOM (see POST /parent-pom/upgrade) before
          the app's MUnit/CI will pass on Java 17.
        items:
          type: object
          properties:
            groupId: string
            artifactId: string
            from:
              type: string
              required: false
            to: string
      headSha:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: Git commit SHA of the HEAD used to derive this plan
      topology:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: Deployment topology descriptor (e.g. blue-green, rolling, canary)
      fileEdits:
        type: FileEdit[]
        required: false
        description: List of individual file-level edits included in this plan

  FileEdit:
    type: object
    description: |
      A single file-level edit computed by assess_app. This mirrors the engine's
      ACTUAL output shape (file / kind / from / to + optional coordinate fields), so
      the fileEdits returned by assess can be round-tripped verbatim into an
      approvedChangePlan without failing request validation. The upgrade worker keys
      off `kind` to decide how to apply each edit.
    properties:
      file:
        type: string
        description: |
          Repository-relative path of the file being edited. Under the default
          app-override strategy (upgrade.pomEditStrategy=appOverride) this is the app's
          OWN module pom — version overrides are written there so sibling modules that
          share a parent/BOM are not affected. Under the legacy inPlace strategy this may
          be a shared parent/BOM pom inherited by other modules (see the warnings array).
      kind:
        type: string
        enum: [pomProperty, depVersion, pluginVersion, munitRuntimeVersion, muleArtifactJson, ciWorkflow, munitArgLines, pomVersion]
        description: |
          Category of edit, which tells the worker how to apply it:
          pomProperty (a <properties> value), depVersion / pluginVersion (an inline
          dependency/plugin version), munitRuntimeVersion (MUnit plugin runtime),
          muleArtifactJson (minMuleVersion + javaSpecificationVersions), ciWorkflow
          (target Java version in the CI workflow), munitArgLines (Tier-0 hygiene:
          strip JPMS --add-opens/--add-exports/--add-modules argLines from MUnit
          plugin blocks that break the embedded MUnit container on Mule 4.9 / Java 17),
          pomVersion (minor-bump the value of the app module's own existing <version>
          tag; emitted only when the upgrade already changes something).
      property:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: For pomProperty/dependency/plugin edits, the Maven property or coordinate key involved
      groupId:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: Dependency groupId (present for depVersion edits)
      artifactId:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: Dependency artifactId (present for depVersion edits)
      pluginGroupId:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: Plugin groupId (present for pluginVersion edits)
      pluginArtifactId:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: Plugin artifactId (present for pluginVersion edits)
      from:
        type: any
        required: false
        description: |
          Current value before the edit. Usually a string (e.g. a version); for
          muleArtifactJson it is an object ({ minMuleVersion, javaSpecificationVersions }).
      to:
        type: any
        required: false
        description: Target value after the edit. Same shape as `from`.
      change:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: Flag/reason indicating why this edit is needed (e.g. the gating rule that triggered it)

  DependencyViolation:
    type: object
    description: |
      A single Java-17 dependency-guard finding, reported by the CI guard which resolves
      the FULL Maven dependency tree (direct + transitive) and validates every Mule
      extension against its Java-17 minimum. Surfaced on the job (see JobStatus.report)
      so callers/agents can show exactly which connector to pin.
    properties:
      groupId:
        type: string
        description: Extension groupId (e.g. org.mule.connectors).
      artifactId:
        type: string
        description: Extension artifactId (e.g. mule-objectstore-connector).
      resolvedVersion:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: The version Maven actually resolved in the tree (may be transitive).
      requiredVersion:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: |
          The Java-17 minimum (floor) the extension must meet, or "unknown" for a Mule
          extension not present in the guard's floors set (reported as a warning).
      reason:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: Why this was flagged (e.g. "below Java 17 minimum").

  AssessmentResult:
    type: object
    properties:
      appName:
        type: string
      currentRuntime:
        type: string
      currentJavaVersion:
        type: string
      changePlan:
        type: ChangePlan
      warnings:
        type: array
        items: string

  JobStatus:
    type: object
    properties:
      jobId:
        type: string
      status:
        type: string
        enum: [PROCESSING, ASSESSING, COMMITTING, COMMITTED, PR_OPEN, MUNIT_FAILED, DEP_GUARD_FAILED, DEPLOYING, DEPLOYED, ROLLED_BACK, CLOSED, FAILED_ASSESS, FAILED_COMMIT, FAILED_CI, FAILED_DEPLOY, FAILED_INTERRUPTED]
        description: |
          Job lifecycle state. Most values are terminal or auto-advancing. MUNIT_FAILED is
          a NON-terminal, human-needed PAUSE: the app's MUnit suite failed in CI. The job
          waits (retained for 30 days) until a human fixes the tests and CI reports a test
          success (via POST /webhook/cd-result with stage=test, result=success), which
          resumes it. While MUNIT_FAILED, nextPollSeconds is large or omitted.
          DEP_GUARD_FAILED is a similar NON-terminal PAUSE: the CI Java-17 dependency guard
          resolved the full dependency tree and found a Mule extension (often a transitive,
          e.g. an old mule-objectstore-connector bundled by another connector) below its
          Java-17 minimum. The offending dependencies are listed in `report`. The job waits
          (retained 30 days) until the connector(s) are pinned and CI reports a
          dependency-guard success (stage=dependency-guard, result=success), which resumes it.
          CLOSED is a terminal state set when the upgrade PR is closed WITHOUT merging
          (the app's lock is released so it can be re-run or reapplied).
      message:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: Human-readable detail or error description for the current status
      nextPollSeconds:
        type: integer
        required: false
        description: Suggested number of seconds to wait before polling again
      prUrl:
        type: string
        required: false
      branchName:
        type: string
        required: false
      prNumber:
        type: integer
        required: false
        description: GitHub pull request number, populated once the PR is opened.
      completedAt:
        type: string
        required: false
      error:
        type: string
        required: false
      report:
        type: DependencyViolation[]
        required: false
        description: |
          Java-17 dependency-guard violations. Present only when the guard ran and found
          offending dependencies (typically alongside status DEP_GUARD_FAILED). Lists each
          Mule extension that is below its Java-17 minimum so the caller knows what to pin.

  CoordinateOverrides:
    type: object
    description: |
      Optional per-request overrides for repository/platform coordinates. When omitted, the
      orchestrator resolves them from the app-registry, then convention defaults. For owner/repo/
      appPath/orgId the registry is authoritative and wins over these overrides; they take effect
      only for apps that are not in the registry.
    properties:
      branch:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: |
          Explicit branch to assess/upgrade for THIS request. Highest precedence — overrides the
          registry default and the repository's discovered default branch. Use when targeting a
          specific feature/release branch.
      owner:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: GitHub owner/org override (used only when the app is not in the registry).
      repo:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: GitHub repository name override (used only when the app is not in the registry).
      appPath:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: Path to the Mule module within the repo (e.g. "." for repo root).
      orgId:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: Anypoint organization ID override (used only when the app is not in the registry).

  CdResultRequest:
    type: object
    description: |
      CD/CI callback that updates a job. ONE endpoint serves three pipeline stages,
      distinguished by `stage`:
        - stage=deploy (default): deployment result from the CD pipeline
          (success -> DEPLOYED, failure -> FAILED_DEPLOY + rollback).
        - stage=test: MUnit (CI test) result. A failure parks the job in MUNIT_FAILED
          (Slack + Jira notified); a later success resumes the parked job.
        - stage=dependency-guard: Java-17 dependency-gate result (full dependency tree,
          incl. transitives). A failure parks the job in DEP_GUARD_FAILED with the
          summarized `report` of offending dependencies (Slack + Jira notified); a later
          success resumes the parked job.
      Authenticated via the X-CD-Signature-256 HMAC header (X-CD-Token accepted as a
      transitional fallback).
    properties:
      jobId:
        type: string
      result:
        type: string
        enum: [success, failure]
      stage:
        type: string
        required: false
        enum: [test, dependency-guard, deploy]
        description: |
          Which pipeline stage this callback reports. Defaults to `deploy` when omitted,
          keeping existing CD callers backward-compatible. Use `test` to report the
          MUnit/CI outcome, or `dependency-guard` to report the Java-17 dependency-gate
          outcome.
      deployUrl:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: Deployment URL (typically present on stage=deploy success).
      error:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: Human-readable failure detail (present on result=failure).
      report:
        type: DependencyViolation[]
        required: false
        description: |
          Summarized Java-17 dependency-guard violations (present on
          stage=dependency-guard, result=failure). Each entry names a Mule extension that
          resolved below its Java-17 minimum, so the orchestrator can persist and surface
          it on GET /jobs/{jobId}.

  AssessRequest:
    type: CoordinateOverrides
    properties:
      appName:
        type: string
      environment:
        type: string
      jiraTicketId:
        type: string
        required: false

  JobRequest:
    type: CoordinateOverrides
    properties:
      appName:
        type: string
      environment:
        type: string
      jiraTicketId:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: |
          Optional. Jira ticket ID to link this migration to. When present, progress/decision
          comments are posted to it and PR/Slack notifications include a link. When absent, the
          job still runs end-to-end with Jira integration simply skipped.
      approvedChangePlan:
        type: ChangePlan
        required: false
        description: |
          Optional, audit-only. The human-approved plan from assess_app, recorded on the job
          record for traceability. The upgrade worker re-runs assessment internally and drives
          the actual edits from its freshly-computed fileEdits — this value is NOT trusted for
          the edits themselves, so omitting it does not change the upgrade outcome.

  ParentPomUpgradeRequest:
    type: object
    description: |
      Request to upgrade a SHARED parent/BOM pom.xml (not an app) so that the connector versions
      it manages meet the Java 17 compatibility matrix. Complements the app upgrade: apps that
      inherit versions from a parent/BOM only receive gating (runtime/java/munit) edits plus a
      connectorGaps warning; this endpoint fixes the connectors at the source. Reads the pom via
      the GitHub Contents API, pins every matrix connector it declares/manages, opens a PR on a
      new branch, and notifies Slack/Jira. Provide `repoUrl` OR `owner`+`repo`.
    properties:
      repoUrl:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: Git URL of the parent/BOM repository (https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>[.git]). Provide this OR owner+repo.
      owner:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: GitHub owner/org (used when repoUrl is not supplied).
      repo:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: GitHub repository name (used when repoUrl is not supplied).
      pomPath:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: Path to the parent/BOM pom.xml within the repo. Defaults to "pom.xml".
      branch:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: Base branch to read from and target the PR against. Defaults to the repo's default branch.
      environment:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: Optional environment label for logging/traceability only — no deployment is performed.
      jiraTicketId:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: Optional Jira ticket to link; a comment with the PR link is posted when supplied.

  ParentPomUpgradeResult:
    type: object
    properties:
      jobId:
        type: string
        description: |
          Tracking id for this parent/BOM upgrade run. Poll GET /jobs/{jobId} to follow its
          status (PR_OPEN when a PR was opened, NO_CHANGE when the pom already met the matrix).
      status:
        type: string
        description: Current job status — PR_OPEN when a PR was opened, NO_CHANGE when nothing changed.
        enum: [PR_OPEN, NO_CHANGE]
      upgraded:
        type: boolean
        description: True when connector version edits were applied and a PR was opened.
      pomPath:
        type: string
        required: false
      branchName:
        type: string
        required: false
      prUrl:
        type: string
        required: false
      prNumber:
        type: integer
        required: false
      jiraTicketId:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: The linked Jira ticket, when one was supplied on the request.
      jiraUrl:
        type: string
        required: false
        description: Clickable Jira link, built when a jiraTicketId was supplied.
      edits:
        type: FileEdit[]
        required: false
        description: |
          The connector/property version edits applied to the parent/BOM pom. When any
          connector is pinned, a trailing pomVersion edit is also included that minor-bumps
          the parent/BOM's own <version>.
      message:
        type: string
        required: false

/parent-pom:
  /upgrade:
    post:
      description: |
        Upgrade a shared parent/BOM pom.xml so the connector versions it manages meet the Java 17
        compatibility matrix, then open a PR. Use this to fix the connectorGaps reported by
        assess for apps that inherit versions from a parent/BOM.
      body:
        application/json:
          type: ParentPomUpgradeRequest
      responses:
        200:
          description: The parent/BOM already meets the matrix; nothing to change.
          body:
            application/json:
              type: ParentPomUpgradeResult
        202:
          description: Connector versions upgraded and a PR was opened against the parent/BOM repo.
          body:
            application/json:
              type: ParentPomUpgradeResult

/jobs:
  /assess:
    post:
      description: Assess a deployed MuleSoft application for runtime and Java version upgrade readiness.
      body:
        application/json:
          type: AssessRequest
      responses:
        200:
          body:
            application/json:
              type: AssessmentResult

  post:
    description: Submit an approved migration job.
    body:
      application/json:
        type: JobRequest
    responses:
      202:
        body:
          application/json:
            type: object
            properties:
              jobId:
                type: string

  /{jobId}:
    uriParameters:
      jobId:
        type: string
    get:
      description: Retrieve the current status of a migration job.
      responses:
        200:
          body:
            application/json:
              type: JobStatus
        404:
          description: No job with the specified jobId exists.
    delete:
      description: |
        Admin / maintenance: permanently delete a job record from the Object Store and
        clear its branch->jobId index entry. Intended for test teardown and manual
        cleanup only — the upgrade lifecycle itself never deletes jobs (they age out via
        the 30-day jobStore TTL). Governed at deploy time (API Manager / gateway policy);
        not part of the normal orchestration surface.
      responses:
        200:
          body:
            application/json:
              type: object
              properties:
                deleted: boolean
                jobId: string
                branchIndexCleared: boolean
                branch:
                  type: string
                  required: false
                lockReleased: boolean
                appName:
                  type: string
                  required: false
        404:
          description: No job with the specified jobId exists.

    /reapply:
      post:
        description: |
          Re-launch an upgrade for the same app using this job's stored inputs (appName,
          environment, jiraTicketId, resolved coordinates), re-assessed against the CURRENT
          compatibility matrix. Primary use: after the matrix was republished to cover a
          connector that was previously left un-pinned, or to retry a MUNIT_FAILED /
          DEP_GUARD_FAILED / FAILED_* / CLOSED job without re-supplying coordinates. Releases
          this job's app lock and mints a NEW jobId for the relaunched run.
        responses:
          200:
            description: The app was already in the desired state; nothing to reapply.
            body:
              application/json:
                type: object
          202:
            description: Upgrade re-assessed and relaunched under a new jobId.
            body:
              application/json:
                type: object
                properties:
                  reapplied: boolean
                  previousJobId: string
                  jobId: string
                  appName:
                    type: string
                    required: false
                  environment:
                    type: string
                    required: false
                  status:
                    type: string
                    required: false
                  message:
                    type: string
                    required: false
          404:
            description: No job with the specified jobId exists.

/webhook:
  post:
    description: Receive GitHub pull request webhook events.
    body:
      application/json:
        type: object
    responses:
      200:
        description: Webhook event received and acknowledged.

  /cd-result:
    post:
      description: |
        Receive CD/CI result callbacks and update job status. Handles both deployment
        results (stage=deploy, the default) and MUnit/CI test results (stage=test).
      body:
        application/json:
          type: CdResultRequest
      responses:
        200:
          description: CD/CI result received and acknowledged.